<article class="env-lemma" id="0GF7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GF7">Lemma <span data-tag="0GF7">69.17.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : Y \to X$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume $f$ is finite, surjective and $X$ locally Noetherian. Let $i : Z \to X$ be a closed immersion. Denote $i' : Z' \to Y$ the inverse image of $Z$ (Morphisms of Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/03MA" data-tag="03MA">67.13</a>) and $f' : Z' \to Z$ the induced morphism. Then $\mathcal{G} = f'_*\mathcal{O}_{Z'}$ is a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ Z$-module whose support is $Z$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Observe that $f'$ is the base change of $f$ and hence is finite and surjective by Morphisms of Spaces, Lemmas <a href="/tag/03MH" data-tag="03MH">67.5.5</a> and <a href="/tag/03ZS" data-tag="03ZS">67.45.5</a>. Note that $Y$, $Z$, and $Z'$ are locally Noetherian by Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/04ZK" data-tag="04ZK">67.23.5</a> (and the fact that closed immersions and finite morphisms are of finite type). By Lemma <a href="/tag/07UH" data-tag="07UH">69.12.9</a> we see that $\mathcal{G}$ is a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ Z$-module. The support of $\mathcal{G}$ is closed in $|Z|$, see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/07TZ" data-tag="07TZ">67.15.2</a>. Hence if the support of $\mathcal{G}$ is not equal to $|Z|$, then after replacing $X$ by an open subspace we may assume $\mathcal{G} = 0$ but $Z \not= \emptyset $. This would mean that $f'_*\mathcal{O}_{Z'} = 0$. In particular the section $1 \in \Gamma (Z', \mathcal{O}_{Z'}) = \Gamma (Z, f'_*\mathcal{O}_{Z'})$ would be zero which would imply $Z' = \emptyset $ is the empty algebraic space. This is impossible as $Z' \to Z$ is surjective. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>